  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>In hydrogen atom <math><mrow><msub> <mtext>E</mtext> <mtext>n</mtext> </msub> <mo></mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac linethickness=\"1\"><mrow><mi>R</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>c</mi></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math><br /><br />where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> is the mass of the electron. Here, the electron has been replaced by a particle whose mass is double of an electron. Therefore, energy in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>n</mi><mi>th</mi></msup></math> orbit for this hypothetical atom will be given by<br /><br /><math><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo></mo><mo></mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac linethickness=\"1\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>c</mi></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math><br /><br />The longest wavelength&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi></math>max (or minimum energy) photon will correspond to the transition of the particle from&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">hc</mtext><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mtext>max</mtext></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msub><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">E</mtext><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">E</mtext><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">Rhc</mtext><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><br />This gives, &lambda;<sub> max</sub><math><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac linethickness=\"1\"><mn>18</mn><mrow> <mn></mn><mn>5</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math></p>"
  }
}